  "title": "CMakeLists.txt: more improvements for Solaris.",
  "description": "The Oracle Studio compiler is stuck at C11, and doesn't seem to be under\nmuch development any more, so it may never get C17. Instead of having\nthat cause an error the first time we try to compile a program when\ntesting, test up front for whether we have C17 and C++17 support and, if\nnot, fail with a simpler error message that gives the underlying problem\nand suggests using GCC or Clang.\n\nIn addition to fixing the way find_package() works when doing a 64-bit\nbuild, we also need to fix the way pkg-config works, by tweaking\nPKG_CONFIG_PATH.",
